A first implementation exposed exactly the kind of construction leak the adversary rules are meant to catch: using \(2\) with Mersenne primes put every planted root in the tiny order of \(2\), yielding conspicuously small answers such as 64. I’m removing that low-order choice and tightening the shipping rung so the disclosed compact route remains under the 300-operation cap.
